course: dictionary
lesson: 2699
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dig can mean making a hole in the ground, or a poke, or a place where people look for old things. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «Long ago tunnels were dug by hand with picks, shovels and gunpowder.» Dug is the past tense of dig, so the tunnels were made by digging through the ground.
explain: «The Terracotta Army near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well.» Here digging means making a hole in the ground, this time to get water. The words well and found are the clues. Always ask: what does this word do in the sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Dig can also be a noun. A dig is a place where archaeologists dig to find old things. Small phrases change the meaning too: dig in means start eating, and dig deep means try very hard. When you meet dig in a new phrase, think about the whole phrase, not just the single word.
fact: Dig means to make a hole in the ground, for example with a spade, with your hands or with paws.
fact: Dig up means to get something out of the ground.
fact: A dig is a place where archaeologists dig to find old things.
fact: A dig can also be a little poke or an unkind remark.
fact: «Dig in» means start eating, and «dig deep» means try very hard.
exercise: «Tenrecs look like hedgehogs or shrews, and they are African animals that dig for ants.» What does dig mean here? | Walk slowly across the grass | Sing loudly to call their friends | Run very fast to escape | *Make holes in the ground to get food
exercise: «Dig in!» said Grandma as the dinner went on the table. What does dig in mean? | Hide under the table | Start digging a hole in the garden | *Start eating | Stop talking and listen
exercise: In «Her dig about my messy room really hurt my feelings», what is a dig? | A spade for the garden | *An unkind remark | A hole in the ground | A meadow full of flowers
test:
Scientists dig up old bones to learn about animals that lived long ago. What does dig up mean? | Bury something deeper | *Get something out of the ground | Read a book about animals | Paint a picture of a bone
Maya said, «I will dig deep and finish my homework tonight.» What does dig deep mean? | Make a big hole in the yard | Go to sleep early | *Try very hard | Eat her dinner quickly
exam:
«Suddenly he throws down his brush and digs his way up into the sunshine of a big meadow.» What does digs mean here? | *Makes a way through the earth | Throws the brush away | Looks up at the sky | Runs across the meadow
